xnu: 0091 sweet skip serial KDP init, keep debug console on fbcon

Real-phone boot #19 (0088+0089+0090 kernel) got further than every
previous boot: kdp_core_init() registered the core dump handler, then
kdp_init() printed "Serial requested, consistent debug disabled or
debug boot arg not present, configuring debugging over serial" and the
machine froze with no further fbcon output.

On arm64 the CONFIG_SERIAL_KDP block in kdp_init() is entered whenever
no kdp_match_name boot-arg is set and no ADT consistent-debug registry
exists (PE_consistent_debug_enabled()).  It registers the serial
send/receive pair, which would route KDP packets through
pal_serial_putc into pe_serial.  Sweet has no usable UART - pe_serial
is the framebuffer fake serial console - so serial KDP can never reach
a debugger and only garbles the one debug channel we have.

Skip the entire serial-KDP registration when building for
ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET, right after kdp_core_init() so the core dump
handler registration is preserved.  printf/kprintf/panic output keeps
flowing through the console path; other arm64 boards are unchanged.
diff --git a/osfmk/kdp/kdp_udp.c b/osfmk/kdp/kdp_udp.c
--- a/osfmk/kdp/kdp_udp.c
+++ b/osfmk/kdp/kdp_udp.c
@@ -2260,6 +2260,19 @@
 	kdp_setup_packet_size();
 	kdp_core_init();
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * P0091: sweet has no usable UART, so serial KDP packets never
+	 * reach a host debugger; the pe_serial frame-buffer fake uart
+	 * would only garble the console, and real-phone boot #19 wedged
+	 * right after "configuring debugging over serial".
+	 * Skip the whole serial-KDP registration here; the debug console
+	 * stays on fbcon and panics keep printing through the console.
+	 */
+	printf("P0091: serial KDP skipped on sweet, debug console stays on fbcon\n");
+	return;
+#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
+
 #if CONFIG_SERIAL_KDP
 	char kdpname[80];
 	struct kdp_in_addr ipaddr;
